# Level 19 -> Level 20

# Objective:
Retrieve the password for bandit20 stored in /etc/bandit_pass/bandit20 using the setuid binary located in the home directory

# breakdown:
The home directory contains a SetUID binary named bandit20-do owned by user bandit20. Running this binary executes any appended command with the elevated privileges of bandit20 rather than bandit19. Passing cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit20 as an argument executes cat under bandit20's authority, granting access to the protected password file.

# Command:
./bandit20-do cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit20
